  "body": "NOW $1,799,000 | 28 RAUTARA STREET, ORAKEI\r\n\r\nTheir next home is purchased. The price has been reduced by $50,000. Their instructions are clear - they want this property SOLD before the end of the year!\r\n\r\nFor buyers seeking exceptional value in Orakei, this is an opportunity that deserves immediate attention.\r\n\r\nForget the age on the title. Behind its 1930s origins lies an extraordinary architectural transformation. This home is virtually new inside and out, with extensive rebuilding, a stunning contemporary extension, designer finishes and beautifully reimagined outdoor spaces.\r\n\r\nAt $1,799,000, the opportunity to secure this level of architectural design, quality and lifestyle in a premium, flat Orakei street is compelling.\r\n\r\nA HOME WITH A STORY\r\n\r\nOriginally a modest 1930s three-bedroom residence, the property caught the eye of its current owner, the daughter of Auckland's renowned Leuschke architectural family.\r\n\r\nHaving grown up in the area, she had always admired this home. When she heard it was coming to market, she and her family literally abandoned their lunch at a local café, raced over to see it and put in an offer that very day.\r\n\r\nThey bought the home they had dreamed about - and set about creating something remarkable.\r\n\r\nWhat followed was far more than a renovation. Virtually none of the original interior remains. The home has been extensively transformed with sleek architectural lines, dramatic black-framed floor-to-ceiling glazing, a sophisticated designer kitchen and beautifully appointed bathrooms with floor-to-ceiling tiling.\r\n\r\nThe former detached garage has been incorporated into the home, creating three bedrooms and a family bathroom in the original wing, flowing through to the dining area and contemporary kitchen.\r\n\r\nThe architectural extension introduces a stunning living room, where walls of glass frame lush bamboo, creating an almost Japanese Zen-like atmosphere. Peaceful, private and wonderfully serene, it's hard to believe you're so close to the city.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the main bedroom offers a beautiful private retreat.\r\n\r\nSUN, SPACE AND PRIVACY\r\n\r\nThe transformation extends outdoors.\r\n\r\nA formerly sloping front garden has been levelled to create a sunny, fully fenced lawn, ideal for children and pets.\r\n\r\nAt the rear, private decking, a spa pool and sun-drenched outdoor living provide the perfect setting for entertaining or simply relaxing. A generous strip of lawn along the side of the home adds further space for family enjoyment.\r\n\r\nThe owners have treasured the extraordinary peace, privacy and sunshine this property offers.\r\n\r\nPREMIUM ORAKEI LOCATION\r\n\r\nRautara Street is a sought-after, remarkably flat street, offering a wonderful combination of residential tranquillity and everyday convenience.\r\n\r\nApproximately a three-minute walk to Orakei School, where both of the owners' children attended.\r\nEasy bus access to Selwyn College.\r\nA nearby walkway connecting to the vibrant Coates Avenue village, with its cafés, restaurant, bar, butcher, hairdresser, post office and local shops.\r\nMinutes from Eastridge Shopping Centre.\r\nClose to the beautiful Eastern Bays beaches.\r\nConvenient motorway connections and easy access to Auckland's CBD.\r\n\r\nTHEIR NEXT CHAPTER HAS BEGUN - NOW IT'S YOUR TURN!\r\n\r\nThe owners have already committed to their next property. They have reduced their asking price by $50,000 to $1,799,000 and are focused on achieving a sale before the end of the year.\r\n\r\nFor buyers comparing renovated older homes with modern architectural residences, this property offers a rare combination: the charm of an established neighbourhood, the feel of an almost entirely new home, exceptional privacy and a premium Orakei address.\r\n\r\nThe money has been spent. The transformation is complete. The vendors are ready to move on.\r\n\r\nNOW ASKING $1,799,000 - SERIOUS SELLERS, SERIOUS OPPORTUNITY.\r\n\r\nDon't wait until the new year to discover what you could have secured today.\r\n\r\nInspect now. Bring your offer. These vendors want to sell!\r\n\r\nTo all agents: Conjunctionals are welcome!",
